  { "kind": "explanation",
    "title": "Vowels and consonants",
    "body": "There are 5 vowels: A, E, I, O, U (Y is sometimes a vowel). The other 21 letters are consonants. English has ~26 letters but roughly 40 distinct sounds, because letters combine to make new sounds like 'sh', 'ch' and 'th'."
  },

  { "kind": "didYouKnow",
    "fact": "The word 'alphabet' comes from the first two Greek letters — alpha (α) and beta (β)." },

